invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: the server seals the connection's original QUIC version into its
  ticket instead of the negotiated one, so a ticket from a connection the
  server moved to version 2 names version 1. RFC 9369 section 5 makes a
  ticket from compatible negotiation belong to the negotiated version
  (rfc9369.txt:268-284). test/quic_loop_ticket_versions.h opens the
  ticket under the server's key and requires version 2, and requires it
  to resume a connection that starts in version 2.

--- old
    c.quic_version = session_quic_version(t);
--- new
    c.quic_version = t->cfg.quic_original_version;
